+
+### Creating a service from a local template
+
+```bash
+serverless create --template-path ../my-template --path my-service
+```
+
+Use a local directory (including a privately cloned repository or an internal path) as the template.
+Files, subdirectories and dotfiles are copied without modifying the source. Without `--path`,
+the template is copied into the current directory. Existing destination files are not overwritten,
+and an explicitly specified destination directory must not already exist.
+When `--path` is supplied, the service is renamed to the destination directory name;
+`--name` overrides that name.
